 "result_text": "`TreeNode.to_dict()` no longer sends the structured metadata fields, so topic nodes should stop triggering Studio's \"must pass a list of values\" error. I only confirmed that `ricecooker.classes.nodes` still imports. I didn't run the tests or try an upload against Studio.\n\n- **Topic nodes:** I removed the six keys that were hard-coded to `None` (`grade_levels`, `resource_types`, `learning_activities`, `accessibility_categories`, `subjects`, `needs`) from `TreeNode.to_dict()`. Studio only checks the fields that are present, so omitting them should be accepted.\n- **Content nodes:** I made the same change to `ContentNode.to_dict()`. A content node that never had a field set (for example `subjects`) would also have sent `null` and failed the same way. It now leaves out any of those six fields that are `None`. Fields you do set are sent as before.\n\nI added a `METADATA_FIELDS` tuple near the top of `ricecooker/classes/nodes.py` to hold the field names. The changes are all in that file.",
